                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'> Master Code:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> A unique identifier assigned to a particular product or item within an inventory or catalog to distinguish and track individual products. It is unique at a regional level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Bar Codes</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>Standardized codes represented by a unique number assigned to the product in a region.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Product Name:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>The name or title given to a specific product or item that identifies and distinguishes it from other products.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Brand Name:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> The name or label that identifies a particular company, manufacturer, or producer of a product.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- PIM L1 Category:</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>The primary category or classification of a product in a Product Information Management (PIM) system, providing a high-level grouping for organizing and categorizing products.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- PIM L2 Category:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>The secondary category or classification of a product in a PIM system, providing a more detailed grouping for organizing and categorizing products within the primary category.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Status:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> The current state or condition of a product, which could indicate its availability, such as ‘In Catalog’, ‘Out of Catalog’ and ‘Off’.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>            -  In Catalog: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>&quot;In Catalog&quot; refers to products or items that are currently available and listed within the catalog or inventory. These products are actively included in the assortment and are ready for sale or display.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>           - Out of Catalog:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> &quot;Out of Catalog&quot; refers to products or items that are not currently available or listed within the catalog or inventory. These products may have been temporarily removed or discontinued from the assortment and are not accessible for sale or display.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>          - </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>Off:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> &quot;Off&quot; typically indicates that a product or item is not in active circulation or available for sale. It may imply that the product has been permanently discontinued, out of stock, or withdrawn from the market. The status &quot;Off&quot; signifies that the product is not actively part of the current inventory or assortment.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Rank Aggregation:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> The desired Rank Aggregation level of the data. You have the option to select either &apos;City&apos; or &apos;Country&apos; to view the top-selling products at a local city level or a broader market level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Revenue / Vendor (EUR):</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>The total amount of revenue generated by a vendor, depicted in euros (EUR), from the sale of products.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Avg. Price Sold (Local Currency):</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>The average price at which a product is sold, expressed in the local currency of the market or region.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Min. Price Sold (Local Currency):</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>The minimum price at which a product is sold, expressed in the local currency of the market or region.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium'>- Percentile 25 price (Local Currency): </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'>The price point below which 25% of the product&apos;s sales prices fall, expressed in the local currency of the market or region.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#606b76' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='4' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='83094' id='6' type-v2='text' w='27417' x='71835' y='15632'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#c42f45' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='15'>How to use:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> 1) Please choose the desired Rank Aggregation level from the dropdown menu. You have the option to select either &apos;City&apos; or &apos;Country&apos; to view the top-selling products at a local city level or a broader market level.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> 2)  Enter the vendor ID for which you would like to see the assortment and receive recommendations.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> 3) Press the enter key, and the initial view will display a comparison between the top-selling SKUs from the previous year and the vendor&apos;s assortment.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Medium' fontsize='8'> 4)To view the comparison of top-selling products from the previous year&apos;s next month, click on view 2.</run>
                    <run>Æ



































</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#606b76' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='4' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{E9DCB020-BB81-4D89-A9D3-9513F5F76815}' />
    </dashboard>
